<title>SINGAPORE: India sells Feb NGL to Glencore, $30.75/T discount.</title>
<headline>India sells Feb NGL to Glencore, $30.75/T discount.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has sold 25,000 tonnes of natural gas liquids (NGL) to Swiss trader Glencore at $30.75 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on a free-on-board (fob) basis, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender which offered the cargo from Hazira on the west coast, closed February 20 and was valid for one day.</p>
<p>A source at Glencore was not able to confirm the award as the company has not received the confirmation.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
</text>
